From: ZCode <agent@local>
Subject: [PATCH] fuxi-keys: three-sample debounce for key state changes

USB unplug perturbs the PMK8550 pon_hlos RT_STS for longer than the old
two-poll (40 ms) debounce: the power bit read as pressed with 0x90 for
two consecutive polls, SweetHID reported a phantom power key, and the
lock sequence ran display-off + SpringBoard relaunch (reported by the
user as "unplug hangs the phone": black screen, spinner, lock screen).
Require three equal samples 20 ms apart (60 ms) before a key state
flips; real presses are unaffected.
---
 bsd/dev/fuxi_keys.c | 27 ++++++++++++++++++---------
--- a/bsd/dev/fuxi_keys.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/fuxi_keys.c
@@ -226,7 +226,7 @@
 fk_thread(void *arg, wait_result_t result)
 {
 	static const char *names[3] = {"power", "volume-up", "volume-down"};
-	int state[3] = {0, 0, 0}, last[3] = {0, 0, 0};
+	int state[3] = {0, 0, 0}, last[3] = {0, 0, 0}, hold[3] = {0, 0, 0};
 	unsigned errors = 0;
 	(void)arg;
 	(void)result;
@@ -249,12 +249,24 @@
 			errors = 0;
 		}
 		for (int k = 0; k < 3; ++k) {
-			/* Two equal samples 20 ms apart before a change counts. */
-			if (ok[k] && now[k] == last[k] && now[k] != state[k]) {
-				state[k] = now[k];
-				printf("FUXI KEYS: %s %s (pon=%#x gpio6=%#x)\n", names[k],
-				    state[k] ? "down" : "up", pon, gpio);
-				sweet_hid_key(k, state[k]);
+			/* Three equal samples 20 ms apart (60 ms) before a change counts: USB
+			 * unplug perturbs the PMK8550 pon RT_STS for two polls and was seen as
+			 * a phantom power key that restarted SpringBoard (unplug hang report). */
+			if (!ok[k]) {
+				continue;
+			}
+			if (now[k] != state[k]) {
+				hold[k] = (now[k] == last[k]) ? hold[k] + 1 : 1;
+				if (hold[k] >= 3) {
+					state[k] = now[k];
+					hold[k] = 0;
+					printf("FUXI KEYS: %s %s (pon=%#x gpio6=%#x)\n", names[k],
+					    state[k] ? "down" : "up", pon, gpio);
+					sweet_hid_key(k, state[k]);
+				}
+			} else {
+				hold[k] = 0;
+			}
 			}
 			if (ok[k]) {
 				last[k] = now[k];
